## Consolidate test projects under tests/

### Status
Implemented.

### GitHub Issue
#112

### Summary
`WhenWorksWeb.Tests` lives at the repo root while `tests/js-unit` holds the JS suite. Move the
xUnit project under `tests/` so all test projects live in one place, and fix a related CI gap
found along the way.

### Motivation
With two test suites now in place (and a UI test project planned later), keeping only one of
them under `tests/` is inconsistent and makes the repo root more cluttered than it needs to be.
Separately, `.github/workflows/dotnet.yml` currently runs `dotnet test` against
`WhenWorksWeb/WhenWorksWeb.csproj` (the app project) rather than the test project, so CI has
never actually run the xUnit suite — worth correcting while touching this workflow's paths
anyway.

### Proposed Changes
- Move `WhenWorksWeb.Tests/` to `tests/dotnet-unit/WhenWorksWeb.Tests/`, keeping the `.csproj`/
  project/assembly name `WhenWorksWeb.Tests` unchanged — only the folder location moves.
- Update `WhenWorksWeb.slnx`'s project path.
- Update `WhenWorksWeb.Tests.csproj`'s `<ProjectReference>` to `WhenWorksWeb/WhenWorksWeb.csproj`
  for the new relative depth.
- Update `.claude/hooks/run-affected-tests.ps1`'s `$testProject` path.
- Update `CODING_CONVENTIONS.md`'s Testing Conventions section's path references.
- Fix `.github/workflows/dotnet.yml` to run `dotnet test` against the relocated
  `WhenWorksWeb.Tests.csproj` instead of the app project.

### Acceptance Criteria
- `dotnet build` and `dotnet test` succeed from the repo root via `WhenWorksWeb.slnx`.
- `.claude/hooks/run-affected-tests.ps1` still locates and runs the test project correctly.
- CODING_CONVENTIONS.md's test file paths are accurate.
- CI's `.NET` workflow actually executes the xUnit suite (not just builds the app project).

### Out of Scope
- The future UI test project and its naming — deferred to a separate issue.
- Any change to `WhenWorksWeb.Tests`'s project/assembly name, internal folder structure, or test
  content.
